course: dictionary
lesson: 5257
title: Jokingly: not meant seriously
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Jokingly is an adverb. It tells you how someone said or did something: in a joking way, not seriously, to be funny. When you read it, ask yourself, "Is the writer really serious here?"
explain: Look at the words around it. «Gave up the ghost» means died, but when it is said jokingly of a machine that has stopped working, it means the machine is broken for good. Nobody is really sad, and the word jokingly is the clue.
explain: Check by taking jokingly out. Does the sentence now sound serious or strange? If it does, jokingly was there to show the words were a joke. Phrases to know are say jokingly, jokingly called, and half jokingly, which means partly a joke and partly serious.
fact: Jokingly means in a joking way, not seriously.
fact: Jokingly is an adverb, so it tells you how something is said or done.
fact: «Gone to meet his maker» means died, and it is often used jokingly.
fact: «Shuffled off this mortal coil» means died; it comes from Shakespeare's Hamlet and is used jokingly.
fact: «Resting» means out of work, said jokingly of an actor (mostly UK).
exercise: Dad says jokingly that the old toaster has «gone to meet his maker». What does jokingly tell you? | The speaker is very angry | The words are a sad, true report | *The words were not meant seriously | The speaker is whispering a secret
exercise: A machine that has «given up the ghost» has stopped working. What does this mean when it is said jokingly? | It has become very quiet and shy | It has been given a ghost to look after | It is ready to start a new job | *It has stopped working for good
exercise: Lily is jokingly called «the Professor» by her friends. What does jokingly mean? | Very slowly and carefully | In a very serious and angry way | *In a joking way, not seriously | In a secret whisper
test: Ben says the «dearly departed» are the dead, and that the phrase is polite and sometimes used jokingly. What are the dearly departed? | People who have just left the room | *The dead | Old family photographs | Very dear friends who visit often
test: An actor says he is «resting», said jokingly. What does resting mean here? | Sitting quietly in the sun | *Out of work | Very tired after a long play | Asleep in bed all day
exam: Which best explains what jokingly means? | In a very slow and sad voice | In a loud, angry shout | In a secret, careful whisper | *In a joking way, not seriously
